Restore the logging MobileFeliCaClient was shipped without

R8 emptied LogMgr's two sinks - log(int,String,Object[],long) and
logArray(int,byte[]) - to "return-void", so every one of the several
thousand call sites in MFC still runs and produces nothing. That leaves
no way to see which branch MFC takes: it reports a failure to the caller
as a numeric FelicaException and says nothing about how it got there.

Fill the two sinks back in against android.util.Log under the tag
"MfcLog". The message itself is built by LogMgr.format(), which R8 left
intact; the caller is recovered from the stack (the first frame that is
not LogMgr itself) because the messages are three-digit markers - "001",
"800" - that only mean something next to the class and method they came
from.

Everything is inside a try/catch that swallows: this is diagnostics, and
it must not be able to turn a working path into a crashing one.

